xtu|n|A round or spherical body, solid or hollow; a body whose surface is in every part equidistant from the center; a ball; a sphere. ; Anything which is nearly spherical or globular in shape; as, the globe of the eye; the globe of a lamp. ; The earth; the terraqueous ball; -- usually preceded by the definite article. ; A round model of the world; a spherical representation of the earth or heavens; as, a terrestrial or celestial globe; -- called also artificial globe. ; A body of troops, or of men or animals, drawn up in a circle; -- a military formation used by the Romans, answering to the modern infantry square.	n:9hq,88,1~9hq,88,1	N:12kw,75,9;aqi,42,2;p3w,23,1~12kw,75,9;aqi,42,2;p3w,23,1
